llenge rather than request a software workaround.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. d3 software architecture / workplan\n\n```text\ninputs\ntask = [software architecture/change problem]\nrepository_target = [repository/worktree/branch to inspect; auto = current repository]\nexisting_authorities = [current d1/d2/d3/d4 authorities and governed contracts; auto = discover]\nworkplan_destination = [d3 change-plan/workplan path; use the d3->d4 implementation-workplan specialization when d4 is affected; auto = repository convention]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = governing declared protocol/version; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = create/update d3 authority/workplan; report_only = inspect/report only]\nadditional_constraints = [optional explicit user constraints; none if absent]\n\nresolve required_skill = software-design. treat d3 as software architecture, not d1/d2 owner. reconcile upstream invariants and domain-local security/reliability/performance/resource/compatibility/deployment contracts.\n\ndesign the minimum justified architecture: cohesive ownership, direct flow, one authoritative representation, fewer interfaces/states/dependencies, removal/consolidation over compensation. keep durable architecture manual authority distinct from cycle-scoped freeze.\n\ncreate/update the d3->d4 workplan when d4 concretization is materially affected. for material d3-only authority mutation needing review, use the generic abstraction-concretization change plan. if current d4 already concretizes accepted d3 and no implementation/review is needed, do not manufacture an empty d4 plan.\n\ndo not modify product implementation. freeze only d3 decisions; leave d4 mechanisms replaceable. define real-owner acceptance, regression/integration, evidence specifications/realizations and execution dependencies, impact closure, and reopen/simplification triggers.\n\nbefore accepted-current durable d3 mutation, require independent pre-acceptance falsification. challenge d3 adequacy against d2 and route d1/d2 defects upward. finish pass/no-pass with any serious challenge first.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. d4 software implementation\n\n```text\ninputs\nchange_plan = [accepted governing change/work plan when one is materially warranted; none only for genuinely local d4-only work under sufficient current authority]\nrepository_target = [repository/worktree/branch to modify; auto = current repository]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = change_plan protocol_version when supplied, otherwise current compatible protocol 6.1 profile; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = modify/test the candidate; report_only = inspect/report only]\nadditional_constraints = [optional explicit user constraints; none if absent]\n\nresolve required_skill = software-implementation under change_plan's declared version; otherwise current compatible protocol 6.1 and accepted d1-d4/external authority. under auto_execute actually modify/test the target.\n\nfor local d4-only work change_plan may be none after proportionate upstream-impact exclusion. direct d1/d2->d4 may use the upstream abstraction-concretization plan plus unchanged d3; do not manufacture d3 mutation.\n\nimplement d4 specification and d3 architecture while preserving d1/d2 and side constraints. treat d4 machinery as replaceable. prefer owning-layer removal/narrowing/rewiring/consolidation over wrappers/fallbacks. do not rewrite specification to bless unintended code.\n\nfor material acceptance distinguish evidence specification/target from evidence realization/observation and execution dependencies. owner-specific evidence follows the final real owner; do not preserve obsolete machinery for a stale harness.\n\nclose every material executable stage with semantic conformance plus focused/stage-local regression. before completion reconcile full contract, inspect obsolete/duplicate/bypass complexity, re-derive affected semantic/evidence/documentation surface, run complete affected regression, real-owner integration/end-to-end, project checks, and bounded impact closure. an unexecuted required check or unresolved required impact is not a pass.\n\nif evidence challenges a parent abstraction, surface serious challenge and stop dependent closure.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. review & challenge pass\n\n```text\ninputs\nworkplan = [governing workplan/change plan]\nimplementation_target = [candidate branch/commit/worktree; auto = current candidate]\nrelated_authorities = [applicable d1/d2/d3/d4 and external authorities; auto = discover]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = governing workplan protocol_version; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = perform review and owned lifecycle updates; report_only = inspect/report only]\nadditional_constraints = [optional explicit user constraints; none if absent]\n\nresolve the parent-boundary owner; normal d4 review uses software-design in independent implementation-review mode. review assembled candidate, not only diff/summary; prefer fresh context for substantial/high-risk work.\n\nfirst challenge pass: test governing authority for consistency, ambiguity, joint concretizability, logical/mathematical coherence, adequacy, abstraction completeness, and simultaneous-authority compatibility. serious challenge is first-line and blocks unqualified pass.\n\nthen reconstruct binding invariants/constraints/cycle freeze/specification and independently falsify concretization fidelity, abstraction adequacy, ownership, science/numerics, reliability/security, resources/performance, affected-surface completeness, oracle strength, evidence applicability/independence, dependency assumptions, impact closure, and complexity.\n\nstale evidence cannot decide the verdict. a partial dependency map cannot establish non-impact without a completeness basis. missing required regression/integration/project checks or unresolved material impacts are blockers.\n\nreview does not modify product implementation, but auto_execute may update/reopen/close its workplan lifecycle record. route d4 nonconformance to implementation, d3 deficiency to software-design, d2 to numerical-algorithm-design, d1 to scientific-formulation.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. verification\n\n```text\ninputs\nverification_scope = [claim/subsystem/workplan/release requiring deeper falsification]\nimplementation_target = [candidate branch/commit/worktree; auto = current candidate]\ngoverning_authority = [applicable accepted d1-d4/external authority; auto = discover]\nscientific_authorities = [d1/d2 authorities; auto = discover; none if genuinely irrelevant]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = governing declared protocol/version; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = execute non-mutating verification; report_only = inspect/report only]\nadditional_constraints = [optional explicit user constraints; none if absent]\n\nperform deeper non-mutating risk-triggered falsification. resolve owning domain skill(s), not software-design by default.\n\nreconcile authorities, construct counterexamples, exercise independent reference/differential/metamorphic/numerical evidence, inspect real semantic-owner paths, and trace executable->d2->d1 closure where material. distinguish internal verification from d1 external adequacy. for high-risk claims inspect common-mode dependence among evidence routes and applicability of each realization.\n\nrun challenge pass. authority contradiction -> serious challenge/human adjudication, not implementation patch or oracle rewrite. verification does not replace review or mutate product implementation.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. stabilization / architecture gc\n\n```text\ninputs\nstabilization_scope = [converged subsystem/workplan/release boundary]\nimplementation_target = [candidate branch/commit/worktree; auto = current candidate]\ngoverning_authority = [accepted d1-d4 authority to preserve; auto = discover]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = governing declared protocol/version; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = perform non-mutating stabilization; report_only = inspect/report only]\nadditional_constraints = [optional explicit user constraints; none if absent]\n\nafter review otherwise passes at a material convergence boundary, inspect whether accepted concretization is still minimum justified: duplicated authority/state, wrappers/fallbacks/special cases, stale compatibility, unnecessary states/config/public surface, ownership leakage/cycles, historical exceptions, dead/bypassed paths, stale concretization-specific evidence, and tests dominated by internal orchestration rather than durable claims.\n\nconsult semantic-evolution history when recurrence suggests an old mechanism/model/test family was materially rejected before. history informs; current authority governs.\n\nstabilization is non-mutating. route justified simplification to d4 under unchanged d3, to d3 when architecture changes, or d2/d1 when evidence exposes upstream defect.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. downstream authority alignment\n\n```text\ninputs\nupstream_accepted_work = [accepted upstream authority/change that altered assumptions]\ndownstream_workplan = [downstream plan/authority to reconcile]\nrepository_target = [repository/worktree/branch; auto = current repository]\ngoverning_authority = [accepted parent invariants and cycle-scoped decisions; auto = discover]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = downstream workplan governing version; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = update owned downstream plan/authority; report_only = inspect/report only]\nadditional_constraints = [optional explicit user constraints; none if absent]\n\nresolve downstream_workplan owner. auto_execute updates the downstream plan/authority when warranted; alignment does not modify product implementation.\n\nreconcile only materially dependent assumptions/invariants/evidence after upstream acceptance. preserve unaffected siblings/still-valid evidence. review evidence specifications separately from old realizations, remap/rerun only changed applicability/execution mappings, and reconcile dependency/history records when triggered.\n\nif upstream change makes downstream abstraction contradictory or impossible to concretize, raise serious challenge instead of a compatibility shim. otherwise make downstream plan snapshot-complete under its own protocol version.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. health audit\n\n```text\ninputs\naudit_scope = [repository/subsystem/history window to assess]\nrepository_target = [repository/worktree; auto = current repository]\nhistory_window = [auto = useful available history; or explicit range]\ngoverning_architecture = [current d3 authority; auto = discover]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = current compatible protocol; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = perform non-mutating audit; report_only = inspect/report only]\nexclusions = [explicit exclusions; none if absent]\n\nresolve required_skill = software-maintenance-audit when available. perform longitudinal sensing, not feature review/approval. combine semantic inspection with real history: churn/change coupling, recurring defect families, complexity, dependency centrality/cycles, public/config growth, weak oracles, stale evidence, documentation difficulty, architecture drift.\n\nmetrics are sensors, not truth; do not fabricate trends from static state. consult semantic-evolution history when useful, without letting history override current authority.\n\naudit does not implement repairs. route d4 local repair to software-implementation, d3 maintenance needing architecture/workplan to software-design, d1/d2 concerns to owners, documentation drift to software-documentation, lifecycle residue to repository-hygiene.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. closeout\n\n```text\ninputs\ncompleted_work = [completed workplan/change-plan/release scope; exact selected workplan may supply this]\nrepository_target = [repository/worktree/branch; auto = current repository]\naffected_documentation = [current docs/generated artifacts/lifecycle records; auto = discover]\nprotocol_source = [auto_local_first = compatible installed skill/root first, then canonical public repository; otherwise explicit source]\nprotocol_ref = [auto = governing completed-work version; otherwise explicit immutable compatible ref]\nexecution_mode = [auto_execute = reconcile documentation/lifecycle artifacts; report_only = inspect/report only]\nadditional_constraints = [optional explicit user constraints; none if absent]\n\ncloseout begins only after semantic/functional acceptance. auto_execute performs documentation, lifecycle, generated-artifact, release/version, dependency/evidence/history, and conservative hygiene reconciliation owned by this stage; it does not change product behavior.\n\nreconcile current d1-d4 authority, guides/runbooks, human-facing background/abbreviation completeness for materially changed current docs, generated artifacts, release/version, current dependency views, affected evidence state, semantic-evolution history when triggered, and completed/superseded workplan state. preserve release-pinned/publication truth.\n\nuse software-documentation for substantive editorial reconciliation and repository-hygiene for proven residue. retire stale evidence/superseded concretizations only when no supported current/compatibility path depends on them and material history is preserved where needed.\n\ncloseout cannot turn unresolved acceptance into completion. an unresolved serious challenge to protocol 6.1 authority blocks protocol 6.1 release.\n```"

